    {
      "id": "claim_3a4a2e64862940b8b5681253ba40535d",
      "statement": "celld runs Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects on your own machines: one node is one celld process, the nodes that share one bucket are a fleet, and a cell is a Durable Object with its own SQLite database whose ownership is decided by a conditional bucket write rather than by membership or consensus.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L14-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b38ea33b7d2476112bec9c830f0bcea697b8beb3d3543387d9c9f48aae44b89e:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://README.md#L3-L11",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28b8ec5c468c5452499f7ee48cd6920279ed6b8710e68656eb77a4056ae4b1bb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_604296b7ea504922aba0c788fbf6e47d",
      "statement": "The workspace is split three ways: crates/logic owns all behavioral state and decisions (a sans-IO decision core), crates/celld is only an effect executor and adapter host, and crates/ltx is the embeddable LTX replication library.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L1-L7",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7ceea2d713120f9935b1ad3899473bfb17dda0caf31fd2ac0eca402cb863818:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7aab8ae164847239cb85d5e7810f05f",
      "statement": "on_event is the only way behavioral state advances: it consumes one Event and returns a list of Effects, and no adapter may mutate State directly; the production executor and deterministic simulator both feed it events and perform the returned effects.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1-L6",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c6004399f0a3eaac4aeafe0ee4b39e82ddf2452e7949f7b56591d1dc72cfe9e1:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L5215-L5215",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:92f95be291fcb6f971dcbe55a0f08e0ff402a7f05be7f4f04c6c5abc504c7f57:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7a8f31e88b084511998a39ba89911875",
      "statement": "The executable runs one serial actor that is the only caller of on_event, polling its mailbox, timers, and in-flight effect futures together in one step; this shape is required so monotonic lease ticks can fence the node even when a storage operation remains hung.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/actor.rs#L2184-L2206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5f8499e3bd120536c944fd168baff88911879401788ac36123287c3f2ec85635:"
